Cross-checked against `/tmp/gitx` — your two requirements match GitX's own implementation exactly (`PBGitHistoryController.m:1105-1137`):

```objc
// Diff with <branch> — own item, disabled when isHead
NSString *diffTitle = ...;
[items addObject:[NSMenuItem pb_itemWithTitle:diffTitle action:@selector(diffWithHEAD:) enabled:!isHead]];
[items addObject:[NSMenuItem separatorItem]];

// Merge / Cherry Pick / Rebase — grouped together, all gated on the same flag
NSString *mergeTitle = isOnHeadBranch ? @"Merge Commit" : [NSString stringWithFormat:@"Merge Commit into "%@"", headBranchName];
[items addObject:[NSMenuItem pb_itemWithTitle:mergeTitle action:@selector(merge:) enabled:!isOnHeadBranch]];

NSString *cherryPickTitle = isOnHeadBranch ? @"Cherry Pick Commit" : [NSString stringWithFormat:@"Cherry Pick Commit to "%@"", headBranchName];
[items addObject:[NSMenuItem pb_itemWithTitle:cherryPickTitle action:@selector(cherryPick:) enabled:!isOnHeadBranch]];
```

So GitX puts a separator before Diff-with-branch, then another separator, then Merge/Cherry-pick/Rebase together as one block — all three gated on the identical `isOnHeadBranch` check. It also relabels the item text dynamically ("Cherry Pick Commit" when disabled vs `Cherry Pick Commit to "main"` when enabled), which is a nice touch worth copying.

For `isOnHeadBranch` itself, GitX computes it by walking their in-memory commit list checking ancestry (`PBGitRepository.m:368`) — we get this for free and cheaper: `CommitHistory.tsx` already fetches `commits.Current` (everything reachable from `currentBranch`), so `commits.Current.some(c => c.id === commitId)` is the direct equivalent, no extra backend call needed. This also confirms the "Diff with `<current branch>`" roadmap item I added earlier matches GitX's real menu item precisely.

Want me to fold the dynamic-label behavior into the plan too, or keep the label static ("Cherry-pick") for simplicity?

